+# E31 (TP4 candidate, cf. vllm#58454): the per-request key/gate tail is a ring of
+# tail_ring slots indexed by position % tail_ring, while the ape/pool phase stays
+# position % 4. A verify step writes 1 + K consecutive positions, including drafts that
+# may be rejected; the open pool's committed members are at most 3 positions before the
+# step, so no row of the step (at most K + 3 positions after a member) can overwrite one
+# when tail_ring >= K + 4. The indexer uses tail_ring = 4 * cdiv(4 + K, 4). With
+# tail_ring = 4, every ring index below reduces to the legacy phase slot: a pool starts
+# at a multiple of 4, so (pool_start + slot) % 4 == slot and position % 4 is the phase.
 
 
